      "why": "`orderService.getOrder` reads through the cache; `placeOrder` validates the items and computes the total before calling the repository.",
      "effect": "Two behaviour changes: cached reads, and 400 for an empty or missing items list.",
      "pseudocode": "getOrder(id):\n  return cache[id] ?? (cache[id] = repo.findById(id))   # only if found\n\nplaceOrder(body):\n  reject 400 unless body.items is a non-empty array\n  repo.create(body + total)",
      "hunks": [
